CORE smt-backend broken-cprover-smt-backend no-new-smt
quantifier-boolean-definition.c
--z3 --trace
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 13 can find 7: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 19 differ: FAILURE$
^  b=(TRUE|FALSE) \(\d\)$
^  c=(TRUE|FALSE) \(\d\)$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
non-constant value
^VERIFICATION ERROR$
--
Z3's solve_eqs preprocessor eliminates a symbol that is defined by a
quantifier, and then returns the quantifier rather than a value from
get-value (see Z3Prover/z3#7743). This must also be worked around for Boolean
symbols that set_to defines directly by a quantifier.
